WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.640
In 1902, William James quoted Vivekananda
in a famous book on religious experience.

2
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:09.910
Vivekananda claimed the
mind has a higher state,

3
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:13.930
beyond reason, where knowledge
beyond reasoning comes.

4
00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:17.280
No one else can step
inside that state to look.

5
00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:21.090
So if a yogi says she has
known Brahman directly,

6
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.390
what could count for or against her claim?

7
00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:28.300
In this mission, you'll put the claim on
a test bench and see what philosophers

8
00:00:28.350 --> 00:00:29.550
bring to it.

9
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:32.310
Then you'll map Hindu
responses to science,

10
00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.960
from conflict to integration.

11
00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:40.350
Your mission: weigh up what could count for
or against a claim to have known Brahman

12
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.250
directly.
